-- erwartet: P001
-- **The paper cut that stands in LINE ONE**, and it was measured on the way to
-- `PLAN-HARDWARE.md` §49 B3: a newcomer writes the file header of the language next door.
--
-- `module m;` is not a notation question. A file header would mean *"everything below is
-- inside this module"* -- a statement about SCOPE, and `moduledecl` says `{ … }` and means a
-- body. **The refusal stays; what was missing was the FORM in the refusal.** Until
-- 2026-09-01 it read `` `{` expected, `;` found `` and nothing else, in front of every other
-- finding of the file, and a reader who does not know the grammar could not read the shape
-- off it.
--
-- The note under the site now carries it. *Nothing became sayable* -- this file falls today
-- exactly as it fell yesterday, and `crates/gabbro-syntax/tests/sprechprobe.rs` holds the
-- note itself, which no poison probe can (the harness matches CODES).
module m;
